            "text": "{\"primary_meaning\":\"The wicked, ungodly, or unfruitful individuals who are separated from the righteous and destined for divine judgment and destruction.\",\"primary_basis\":[\"Psalm 1:4\",\"Matthew 3:12\",\"Luke 3:17\",\"Daniel 2:35\",\"Hosea 13:3\"],\"alternatives\":[{\"meaning\":\"Worthless deeds, earthly works, or empty religious rituals that hold no eternal value and will be consumed by God's testing fire.\",\"basis\":[\"1 Corinthians 3:12-15\"],\"prominence\":\"common\"},{\"meaning\":\"False teachings, false prophecies, or deceptive words, heavily contrasted with the true, nourishing word of God (the wheat).\",\"basis\":[\"Jeremiah 23:28\"],\"prominence\":\"minority\"}],\"has_settled_consensus\":true,\"confidence\":\"high\",\"notes\":\"The symbolism of chaff is remarkably consistent throughout the Bible. It relies on the ancient agricultural practice of winnowing, where harvested grain is tossed into the air so the wind can blow away the light, worthless outer husks (chaff) while the heavy, valuable grain (wheat) falls to the threshing floor. It universally denotes worthlessness, impermanence, and impending judgment.\"}",
